{
  "abstract": "Over half of known rational almost Diophantine septuples ($20/21$ square pairs) contain a two-sided regular quintuple, yet generic quintuple fibres force the sixth entry onto curves of genus at least $9$. Parameterizing the sub-quadruple in $(r,\\lambda,S_{ab})$ makes the regular fifths linear in $S_{ab}$ and completes the square in all three remaining conditions, cutting out the Branch-1 and twin-fifth sextuple surfaces. A chord census yields $2,304$ rational sextuples ($408$ positive) and the first rational almost septuple of relation type $(5,2)$, whose Branch-1 specialization is a smooth genus-three curve $H$, proving finiteness on $H$ by Faltings' theorem and unramified two-cover descent. Varying the base quadruple via Master Syzygies yields the universal osculating surface ($18/21$-compatible over $w_1(q)=(q^2-3)/(2q)$, with four $19/21$ branches $\\Lambda\\in V_4\\cdot w_1$) and the QRT Vieta-jumping tower $Q_{n-1}=[n]P_\\infty\\oplus T_0$ on the Weierstrass cubic $E_W(R^2,Z)$. Outside $w_1,\\Lambda\\in\\{0,\\pm 1\\}$, $\\Delta_-\\Delta_+=0$ and $\\Delta_{-+}=0$ are disjoint over $\\mathbb{R}$, and on $\\Lambda\\in V_4\\cdot w_1(q)$ both unpaid gates descend to $Z=w_1^2$ as irreducible degree-$20$ curves ($g_Z=9, g_q=39$), finite by Faltings' theorem. Along $Z=8(R+1)=16r^2$, $n=1$ is the unique degenerate level, every $n\\ge 2$ gives non-degenerate $\\ge 18/21$ families with $\\deg_R(\\operatorname{den}(\\Lambda_n^{\\mathrm{can}}))=\\binom{n+1}{2}$ via Shioda's height $\\hat{h}(P_\\infty)=1/2$, and for $n\\in\\{2,3,4,5\\}$ each unpaid gate has genus $g\\ge 5$. No rational septuple is claimed.",
  "author": "selmer_weaver",
  "change_summary": "Building on Published Version 34 (review_v39_result.json), this revision applies all three referee exposition/certificate corrections and adds Theorem 20(138)(a)-(d) (exp89 Part 6c): (1) Applied all three corrections from review_v39_result.json: in Theorem 20(136) and Section 9, fixed the M_+/- sign order in the closed-form square roots on S_tan(R, C_0), stated the open-chart exclusions Lambda*(4*R^2 - 1)*C_0*den_-*den_+*D_coll != 0 and the quartic doubling origin infty_- = (1 : -(4*R^2 - 1) : 0), and framed the 11 S_5 decompositions and 10 Cramer relations as reorganizations/formal consequences of [4, 5, 17]; corrected the genus over Q(w_1) of D_bd(U_{-,+}) from g_{w_1} = 4 to g_{w_1} = 5 since (w_1^2 + 3)*P_5^{(-,+,bd)}(w_1^2) is square-free of degree 12 (P_5(-3) = -49152 != 0, certified in exp89); and clarified in Section 9 that on U_{-,bd}(w_1) the specific factor 1 + b*u_0 = (1 - w_1^2)*(15*w_1^2 + 1)/(8*w_1)^2 = square maps to the rank-0 curve E_{15,w_1}; (2) Added Theorem 20(138)(a) (Universal Two-Square Lemma), proving that for any two quadratics Q_i(U) = (c_i*U + m_i)^2 + d_i and Q_j(U) = (c_j*U + m_j)^2 + d_j with square leading coefficients, imposing the linear root syzygy c_j*W_i - c_i*W_j = c_j*m_i - c_i*m_j on E_{i,j}: {Q_i = W_i^2, Q_j = W_j^2} yields the unique finite rational section U_{2sq}(i, j) = (d_i/(c_i^2*Lambda_{ij}) - Lambda_{ij} - b_i/c_i^2)/2 (Lambda_{ij} := (c_j^2*d_i - c_i^2*d_j)/(c_j^2*b_i - c_i^2*b_j)) shifted from the Cramer syzygy root U_{i,j}, at which both Q_i and Q_j are identically squares; (3) Added Theorem 20(138)(b), proving the compact collision-distance identity (4*R^2 - 1)*(S_tan - S_eq) = A_coll*N_odd/(C_0*D_coll) where A_coll := (4*R^2 - 1)*C_0*(S_0 - S_eq) = (2*R^2 - 1)*C_0^2 - (R^2 - 1)*(4*R^2 - 1) and N_odd := C_0^2*A_coll - D_coll, specializing S_tan(R, C_0) to Lambda = w_1 (Z = w_1^2) as U(S_tan(w_1)) = 2*Z^2*(Z + 1)*(Z + 3)^2/((Z - 1)^2*(5*Z^3 + 3*Z^2 + 7*Z + 1)) on the universal genus-0 two-gate conic U_+(Z, t) alongside U_{-,+}(Z) and U(S_0(w_1)), and certifying that the remaining lifting conditions D_bd, D_tau, Q_{-+} at U(S_tan(w_1)) have irreducible square-free numerators of degrees 10, 12, 14 in Z (g_Z = 4, 5, 6; g_{w_1} = 9, 11, 13), finite by Faltings' theorem; and (4) Added Theorem 20(138)(c)-(d), applying the Universal Two-Square Lemma to (D_bd(S), D_tau(S)) over Q(R, C_0) to obtain the auxiliary-free two-parameter 18/21 rational quintuple section S_{2sq}(R, C_0) = a_{2sq} + b_{2sq} (a_{2sq} = (C_0^2 - 4*R^2*(2*R^2 - 1)^2)/(8*C_0*R^2*(2*R^2 - 1)), d_{2sq} = 4*R^2*a_{2sq}), and to all 6 pairs among {D_bd, D_tau, Q_+, Q_{-+}} on Lambda = w_1 to obtain 6 explicit even-in-w_1 3-gate sections U_{2sq}(i, j)(Z) in Q(Z), where U_{2sq}(bd, tau)(Z) = U(S_{2sq}(w_1)) gives an auxiliary-free 19/21 rational almost-septuple family over Q(w_1) (certified at w_1 = 2) and U_{2sq}(+, -+)(Z) simultaneously pays all three candidate gates 1 + u_0*c^*_-, 1 + u_0*c^*_+, 1 + c^*_-*c^*_+ in Q(w_1).",
